You want me to combine these two into 1?

> But more important I personally find the Telephony menu being already cluttered with things not related to telephony

What I see in a recent build are:

* VoIP Calls - as far as I know, VoIP is "IP telephony" of various sorts;
* ANSI - I presume that refers to [Digital AMPS](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_AMPS), i.e. TIA/EIA IS-54 and IS-136, with the [TIA](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telecommunications_Industry_Association) being ANSI-accredited so at least ANSI-adjacent, so it's telephony;
* GSM - obviously telephony;
* IAX2 Stream Analysis - [IAX2](Inter-Asterisk eXchange) is telephony;
* ISUP Messages - [ISUP](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISDN_User_Part) is part of SS7, so telephony;
* 3GPP Uu - obviously telephony;
* MTP3 - more SS7, so telephony;
* [Osmux](https://www.osmocom.org/projects/cellular-infrastructure/wiki/OSmux) - telephony;
* RTP - *used* in some telephony, but not, as far as I know, solely used in telephony, so maybe it belongs elsewhere;
* RTSP - ditto;
* SCTP - "Originally intended for Signaling System 7 (SS7) message transport in telecommunication" according to the Wikipedia page, but, as far as I know, not solely for telephony, so perhaps ditto;
* SMPP operations - if "short messages" are considered solely telephony, it's telephony;
* UCP - more short message stuff, so see above;
* F1AP - sounds cell-phonish to me;
* NGAP - ditto;
* E2AP - ditto;
* H.225 - VoIP, so...;
* SIP Flows - SIP sounds telephonic;
* SIP Statistics - see previous;
* WAP-WSP Packet Counter - WAP was for mobile phones, but it was a way to do Web stuff on them, so maybe it's not strictly telephony.

The menu is somewhat cluttered, although no obviously more so than the main Statistics menu, so the underlying problem appears to be "Wireshark offers too many statistics". :-)

